. 
. * Author: Larissa Giardini Simões
. 
. * ============================
. * Setup
. * ============================
. 
. * clear all
. version 14

. set maxvar 10000


. 
. * INSTALL PACKAGES
. 
. *ssc install ivreg2, replace
. *ssc install ranktest, replace
. 
. * CONFIGURE FILE PATHS * (Please do not change)
. /*
> * the following code automatically sets paths based on where you saved the di
> stributed file-package on your system *
> if strpos("`c(pwd)'", "code") {
>     global ROOT "`c(pwd)'/.."
> }
> else {
>     global ROOT "`c(pwd)'"
> }
> global IN "$ROOT/data/raw" // folder, in which the original datasets are stor
> ed
> global DATA "$ROOT/data/derived" // folder for datasets
> global OUT "$ROOT/out" // folder for output (results, tables)
> 
> */
. 
. * ============================
. * Data Preparation
. * ============================
. 
. * LOAD AND MERGE DATA * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         use "$IN/ppathl.dta", clear // use ppathl as a starting dataset
(SOEP-Core, v37 (EU Edition), doi:10.5684/soep.core.v37eu)

. 
.         * Merge ppathl with all datasets, that you deem relevant for your ana
> lysis. (Tip: use keepusing() to specify which variables to keep from the usin
> g dataset; the default is all.)
. 
.         * biobirth contains information on fertility history
.         merge m:1 pid using "$IN/biobirth.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable pid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(variable cid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(variable gebjahr was int, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(label sex already defined)
(label sex_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

.         * pgen contains user-friendly data on the individual level that are c
> onsolidated from different sources
.         merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pgen.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable syear was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

.         * pl contains all variables from the individual questionnaire
.         merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pl.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable inputdataset was str6, now str9 to accommodate using data's values)
(label cid_EN already defined)
(label pid_EN already defined)
(label cid already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

.         * hgen contains generated variables on household level from the house
> hold interview; use for household net income
.         merge m:1 hid syear using "$IN/hgen.dta", nogen keep(master matches) 
> keepusing(hid syear hghinc)
(label iyear already defined)
(label iyear_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                           663,123  
    -----------------------------------------

. 
.         label language EN // change language of the labels to English

. 
.         save "$DATA/h3_dataset.dta", replace // save merged dataset
file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived_confi
    > dential/95%-sample/h3_dataset.dta saved

. 
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * FILTERS * 
.  
.         gen haspartner = 1 if partner>=1 & 4>=partner
(249,474 missing values generated)

.         replace haspartner = 0 if partner==0 
(246,655 real changes made)

.         keep if haspartner==1/*the gender equality behavior in the household 
> is measured among couples*/
(249,474 observations deleted)

.         gen age = syear - gebjahr

.         keep if age >= 18 & age <= 60
(102,130 observations deleted)

.         keep if sumkids >= 1
(42,075 observations deleted)

. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES * 
. 
.         * Has at least one daughter
.         gen hasdaughter = 0

.         replace hasdaughter = 1 if kidsex01 == 2 | kidsex02 == 2 | kidsex03 =
> = 2 | ///
>     kidsex04 == 2 | kidsex05 == 2 | kidsex06 == 2 | kidsex07 == 2 | ///
>     kidsex08 == 2 | kidsex09 == 2 | kidsex10 == 2 | kidsex11 == 2 | ///
>     kidsex12 == 2 | kidsex13 == 2 | kidsex14 == 2 | kidsex16 == 2 | ///
>     kidsex17 == 2 | kidsex18 == 2 | kidsex19 == 2
(195,146 real changes made)

.         
.                 
.         * The first kid is a daughter
.         gen first_daughter = .
(269,444 missing values generated)

.         replace first_daughter = 1 if kidsex01 == 2
(132,369 real changes made)

.         replace first_daughter = 0 if kidsex01 == 1
(136,857 real changes made)

.         
. 
.         * Education
.         rename pgisced97 educ_aux

.         gen educ = .
(269,444 missing values generated)

.         replace educ = 1 if inlist(educ_aux, 0, 1, 2)
(28,311 real changes made)

.         replace educ = 2 if educ_aux == 3
(105,950 real changes made)

.         replace educ = 3 if educ_aux == 4
(18,656 real changes made)

.         replace educ = 4 if educ_aux == 5
(17,181 real changes made)

.         replace educ = 5 if educ_aux == 6
(55,852 real changes made)

.         label define educlabel 1 "low" 2 "middle voc" 3 "voc + ab" 4 "higher 
> voc" 5 "higher educ"

.         label values educ educlabel

. 
.         * Income
.         gen hhnetincome = hghinc if hghinc >= 0
(43,754 missing values generated)

.         gen log_hhnetincome = ln(hhnetincome)
(43,757 missing values generated)

.         
.         
.         * Housework
.         rename pli0044_h hchildcare 

.         rename pli0043_h hhousework

.         rename pli0040 herrands

.         rename pli0049_h hrepairs

.         *too many missing in the weekend, considering only weeddays
.         
.         replace hchildcare=. if hchildcare<0
(10,009 real changes made, 10,009 to missing)

.         replace hhousework=. if hhousework<0
(10,631 real changes made, 10,631 to missing)

.         replace herrands=. if herrands<0
(13,859 real changes made, 13,859 to missing)

.         replace hrepairs=. if hrepairs<0
(9,175 real changes made, 9,175 to missing)

. 
.         gen hworktotal = hchildcare + hhousework + herrands + hrepairs 
(67,410 missing values generated)

. 
.         *calculating the holsehold total of housework
.         bysort cid syear (hworktotal): egen hhworktotal = total(hworktotal)

.  
.         *calculating shares
.         gen female_hwork = hworktotal if sex == 2
(160,634 missing values generated)

.         bysort cid syear: egen femaletotalhwork = total(female_hwork)

.         gen female_hwork_share = femaletotalhwork / hhworktotal
(53,386 missing values generated)

. 
.  
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 *
. 
. 
.         * The hypothesis is that having daughters (hasdaughter) leads to grea
> ter couples’ gender equality in measured by behaviors. The behovior in questo
> n is the chare os domestic work done by women. 
.         * I was asked to do a causal inference, so not a regular correlation 
> analysis.
.         * Accordingly, I use as a instrument a variable that affects whether 
> someone has a daughter but does not directly affect gender equality behavior.
.         * This variable here is  the sex of the first child since whether the
>  first child is a girl is random.
.         * The IV estimator is a two-stage least square with clustered SEs reg
> ression analysis with female_hwork_share as dependent variable and the dummy 
> variable hasdaughter as independent variable.
.         * This choice is based on the folloing property of the model: uses a 
> time-invariant instrument, that accounts for repeated observations via cluste
> ring, 
.         *includes year fixed effects to control for time trends and is valid 
> even with a long panel.
.         
.  /* reg female_hwork_share hasdaughter [aweight=phrf]
>     reg female_hwork_share hasdaughter hhnetincome i.educ age i.sex [aweight=
> phrf]
>         ivregress 2sls female_hwork_share (hasdaughter = first_daughter) i.ed
> uc age i.sex log_hhnetincome [aweight=phrf] /*IV estmation*/
>         *other tests
>         xtset pid syear /*cosidering the panel structure*/
>         xtivreg female_hwork_share (hasdaughter = first_daughter) i.educ age 
> i.sex log_hhnetincome, re /*random fffects*/
> */      
.         ivreg2 female_hwork_share (hasdaughter = first_daughter) i.educ age i
> .sex log_hhnetincome i.syear [aweight=phrf], cluster(pid) /*Pooled 2SLS with 
> clusterd SE*/
(sum of wgt is     4.2274e+08)

